# Electrum data .gitignore

# macOS artifacts
._*
.DS_Store

# Windows artifacts
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db

# Temporary files
*.tmp

# Electrum runtime artifacts
/blockchain_headers
/cache/
/certs/
/daemon
/daemon_rpc_socket
/forks/
/plugins/
/recent_servers
/config
/wallets/
/testnet/
/testnet4/
/regtest/

# Launcher artifacts
# The launchers under macos/scripts/electrum/ and linux/scripts/electrum/
# each bind a unix socket here, and release it, to learn whether the
# filesystem can hold the one Electrum's daemon needs. Each removes it on
# every branch of that test, so it is left behind only where the launcher
# dies between the bind and the removal. The suffix is the launcher's
# process id.
#
# One name across both platforms: it identifies the same artifact of the
# same test, and nothing in it is language-specific. It is kept shorter
# than daemon_rpc_socket so the test is never the more fragile of the two.
# A socket address holds a path of fixed width, so a probe name longer
# than the one Electrum binds refuses the datadir across a band of
# mount-point lengths in which Electrum's own path still fits.
/.probe.*
